Subject: [PATCH 01/11] Delve tab: fossil prices, biome ranking, boss value per
 kill
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three views. Biomes ranks what a delve level of each biome is worth —
mostly its one exclusive fossil node (Crystal Spire, Humid Fissure,
Molten Cavity...), which is the reason biome choice matters at all —
and shows how much of the mine that biome occupies at your depth from
poewiki's spawn weights. Fossils is the price list those numbers are
built from, plus resonators and per-node values. Bosses covers
Ahuatotli, Kurgal and Aul.

The boss view leads with the MEDIAN kill, not the mean. You get a
handful of these a league, not thirty in a row, and Ahuatotli's ~315c
average is carried by a 16% Doryani's Machinarium: 17% of kills drop
nothing off the table and half come in under ~95c. Each card shows the
p10-p90 spread from a seeded 4000-trial sim with the mean marked on it.

Delve bosses are declared in bossData.js's group shape and priced by its
computeBoss, so there is one drop engine in the codebase, not two.

Fact vs assumption is kept explicit. Biome pools, depth thresholds, the
six exclusive nodes, boss minimum depths and the sampled 3.25.0 n=100
drop rates come from poewiki. How many fossils a node drops, how many
nodes a delve has and how often a city carries its boss are published
nowhere, so they are editable knobs, badged as such, and neither fossil
prices nor boss EVs depend on them. A drop the wiki names but never
rated (Aul's Desecrated Virtue) carries a rate of zero rather than a
plausible guess that would quietly inflate the EV. Weight ramps are
smoothstepped between the wiki's two endpoints and labelled approx there.

fetch-data.mjs now snapshots fossils.json and resonators.json per league
so both lists get self-history and % badges; the tab falls back to
prices.json for older snapshots and just loses the trend arrows.

scripts/test-delve.mjs: 28 tests over dataset integrity and hand-checked
arithmetic fixtures.

