Subject: [PATCH 04/11] Delve: share the real price chart, lead with fossils
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Delve tab was showing tables where the rest of the site shows a
graph. Rather than build a lookalike, the chart moves out of App.jsx
into src/PriceChart.jsx and all four callers use it: the mechanic
panel's set total, the category tabs, and now the fossil list and the
biome curve. App.jsx loses ~200 lines of duplicated Recharts config and
the day/rate/percent helpers move with it.

Fossils & resonators is now the first view, with the same furniture as
Astrolabes and Catalysts — sort, change window, filter, one chart, one
grid — because it is the same question asked of different items.
Fossils are tinted by their biome and badged for node-only and
wall-locked.

Opening a biome now gets the mechanic-panel treatment: its value per
delve charted across the league with its fossils beside it, tap to
overlay, and the existing breakdown kept underneath. biomeValueSeries()
re-runs the whole biome formula against each day's prices, so the curve
answers "is this biome getting better to run" rather than "did fossils
go up". City biomes return no curve at all — their value is their boss,
and a drop table has no price history, so a flat line would be a lie.

Verified the two existing chart callers render identically after the
extraction.

