MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Desecrated Virtue is a divination card, so poe.ninja prices it like any
other and always has — DivinationCard is already in the price map. What
was missing was never the price, only the drop RATE: the wiki lists it
in Aul's drop table but leaves it out of the n=100 rate list.

Which is itself information. Zero sightings in 100 kills is not "no
data" — by the rule of three it puts a 95% ceiling of about 3% on the
rate. The line still defaults to 0 so nothing invented lands in the EV,
but it now carries `sampleZero: 100` and the row offers "use <=3%" as a
one-click value, with the reasoning in the tooltip.

