Subject: [PATCH 07/11] Delve: resonators share the fossil graph, keep their
 own list
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

One chart, two lists. Clicking a resonator plots it in the same graph a
fossil does — the history was already loaded, it just had nowhere to go,
so resonators were a bare table next to a chart that ignored them.

They stay in a separate block under the fossil grid with their own
heading, so sorting or filtering either list never reorders the other,
which is the point of keeping them apart. The filter now covers both;
the sort applies within each. Row labels drop the redundant " Resonator"
(the heading says it) so the socket badge fits on one line.

Also gives the fossil chart the same treatment the biome panel got: no
220px empty box before any history exists.

