From 7e0ac7fccd8993a55ee34912f57311d5f31e06a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 18:20:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] Delve: quote biomes per node, not per delve
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"389c /delve" on a biome card was two claims stacked: what a node pays,
times how often you find one. Only the first is knowable. The second was
a number I invented, it was about 3x too generous, and no label fixes a
figure whose biggest input is a guess.

So the unit changed rather than the wording. A biome is now worth the
node you steer into it for — its Crystal Spire, its Humid Fissure, its
boss — and the three per-delve frequency knobs are deleted along with
the unit that needed them. What remains is price x count: the count is
still an assumption, but a small checkable one ("a Crystal Spire drops
about three Hollow Fossils") rather than a frequency nobody can observe.

The toolbar now quotes what an ordinary fossil node pays at your depth,
weighted by which biomes spawn there — the shares are the wiki's own
spawn weights, so that figure is nearly assumption-free. The biome cards
read /biome, the panel names the node it is quoting, and the curve
charts that node over the league.

Tests pin the new shape: the headline is the biome's own node, a city's
node is one boss kill, feeding a stale per-delve setting moves nothing,
and sanitizeSettings drops those keys rather than carrying them forward.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ERdvL4QxcxEM9GTbJLR9Db
