From e4f3a0c1619e42609df9a7365e95839ffd839841 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 18:27:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] Delve: badge where each assumption came from, lower the
 unsourced ones
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two of the node-count assumptions have somebody's counted figure behind
them and three do not, and until now they all rendered identically. They
don't any more: each carries a `source` and the panel badges it `seen`
or `guess`, with the basis in the row's tooltip.

  seen   3 special fossils per biome node (a delve guide states "about
         three on average"), 5 per smuggler's cache (counted on camera
         at ~5 for ~100c). One delver, no sample size — evidence, thin.
  guess  common fossils alongside, fossils per generic node, boss node
         per city biome. Nothing published, nothing observed.

The guessed ones drop: 2 -> 1, 3 -> 2, and bossPerCity 0.5 -> 0.25. The
rule is that an unsourced number errs toward understating a biome — the
tab should never talk you into a farm. A test pins that ordering, so a
guess can't quietly grow past its sourced neighbour.

