The same checkbox the scarab and category tabs carry, wired the same
way: badges switch to the change*R series with a small div marker, the
chart gains the dashed chaos-per-divine line on its own right-hand axis,
and the drag readout reports nominal and real side by side.

Fossils are the case that most needs it. They have run up hard this
league while the divine has too, and a chaos-quoted +20% does not tell
you whether a fossil gained or the divine simply left it behind. The
banner names the divine's own drift over the selected window so the
answer is on screen rather than inferred.

Rate curve and change*R fields go missing independently — a snapshot
older than the rate feature has prices but neither — so they are checked
separately: the checkbox disables without a curve, and the banner says
when badges predate the stored rate instead of silently staying nominal.

