From c4e5698517651d629a6c6cbfa5f35138565bd3df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 22:13:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] Delve: divine-adjusted readiness is per window, not one
 flag
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Ticking Divine-adjusted on the fossil list did nothing, and the reason
was mine. I gated the badges on a single "does any change*R exist"
flag, but change*R arrives one window at a time: a 24h figure needs a
snapshot from 24h ago that stored the divine rate. Fossils are a new
category, so their self-history starts at zero — the live data is seven
hours old and carries change4R and nothing longer. change24 is there
regardless, because that one comes from poe.ninja's sparkline rather
than our history, so the row looked populated while the toggle sat
inert on the default 24h window.

Readiness is now computed per window. Ticking the box moves you to the
longest window that actually has adjusted data, windows without it dim
with an explanation on hover, and the banner names which are ready and
why the rest aren't — with the real cause (history is Nh old), not the
"these snapshots predate the rate" line, which was the wrong diagnosis
for this case.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ERdvL4QxcxEM9GTbJLR9Db
